---
import PageLayout from '../../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { AUTHOR_NAME, CONTACT_EMAIL, LAST_UPDATED, SITE_NAMES } from '../../data/site-config';
import { route } from '../../i18n/routes';
const lang = 'en';
---
<PageLayout title={`Editorial policy of ${SITE_NAMES[lang]}: sources, tests, corrections`} description="Which pay circulars, pay documents and pension tables Pay Band Calc uses, which sources it refuses, how awards still to come are shown, how the engines are tested and how errors are fixed." lang={lang} noindex={true} breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'Editorial policy' }]} showAuthor={false}>
  <div class="prose prose-slate max-w-none">
    <h1>Editorial and corrections policy</h1>
    <p>Nurses, healthcare staff and teachers use these figures to check a payslip, weigh a new post or plan a career and a retirement. A scale of the wrong year or a pension tier from last April changes the answer, so every figure on the site points back to the body that set it.</p>
    <h2>Who is responsible</h2><p>{AUTHOR_NAME}, reachable at <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.</p>
    <h2>The sources we use</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>for NHS pay: NHS Employers, the Welsh Government’s pay letters, gov.scot and the Department of Health in Northern Ireland, with the NHS terms and conditions handbook for supplements, unsocial hours and overtime;</li>
      <li>for teacher pay: the School Teachers’ Pay and Conditions Document of the Department for Education, the reports of the School Teachers’ Review Body, the SNCT handbook, the Welsh pay document and the Northern Ireland determinations;</li>
      <li>for pensions: NHSBSA, Teachers’ Pensions, the SPPA, the HSC Pension Service and the Department of Education in Belfast, with the scheme regulations on legislation.gov.uk;</li>
      <li>for tax: HMRC’s rates and thresholds for employers and GOV.UK.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>Sources we refuse</h2><p>Unofficial pay calculators, recruitment sites, forums and news articles never provide a figure here, however well they rank. In October 2026 several of them still showed 2025/26 NHS scales or contribution tiers as current. Union pages are read for context but a figure is taken only from the official document.</p>
    <h2>Awards not yet published</h2><p>An award that has been announced but not printed in a scale, such as the Northern Ireland NHS award for 2026/27 or the Welsh teacher award of September 2026, is shown as still to come, with what is known and the date. The site never applies an announced percentage to make up a scale.</p>
    <h2>Testing</h2><p>Every build runs the engine tests: published figures such as the inner London band 5 total of NHS Employers and the M1 and U3 points of the pay document, the tier boundaries of NHSBSA and Teachers’ Pensions, income tax in the rest of the UK and in Scotland, NI, student loans, career average accrual and the lump sum. A failing test stops the build.</p>
    <h2>Review cycle</h2><p>NHS scales change in April, teacher scales in September (August in Scotland), pension tiers and tax thresholds in April. We re-read the parameter file at each of those dates and whenever a circular is issued. Each page shows the date the sources were last read.</p>
    <h2>Corrections</h2>
    <ol><li>We open the official document again.</li><li>We correct the parameter file or the engine, and add a test for the case.</li><li>The pages rebuild and show the new date.</li></ol>
    <h2>Independence</h2><p>No employer, union, pension provider, adviser or government body pays for or reviews what is published here, and the site carries no affiliate link. See also the <a href={route('method', lang)}>method</a>. Version: {LAST_UPDATED}.</p>
  </div>
</PageLayout>
